          <Pad Id="vEzKwlC5CfjgXyrqpEstsk" Bounds="85,85,520,94" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Input (String) [Qt]&#xD;&#xA;- Channel: binds the text, the user writes back (IOBox &quot;Hello&quot; = start value)&#xD;&#xA;- Placeholder: shown while the field is empty&#xD;&#xA;- Editable: off makes the field read-only&#xD;&#xA;- Value: current text; Has Changed: true for one frame when the user committed a change">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="qTVlRuzTzIyLcpV733uB7k" Bounds="85,1009,830,134" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- A plain value or an IOBox on Channel is the start value and sets the text from the patch.&#xD;&#xA;- The typed text is committed on Enter or when the field loses focus, and only when it changed.&#xD;&#xA;- Enter keeps the focus; a click or tap anywhere else in the window commits and leaves the field, Esc discards the edit and leaves it.&#xD;&#xA;- Setting the channel from the patch while the user is typing replaces what was typed.&#xD;&#xA;- Labels come from a Labeled element around each text field (here a Column stacks the Labeled fields).">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
